  {
   "id": "LY3cvHQaFwAJ",
   "from": "Milena Stefanovic",
   "author": "06b643fe2eafa42b",
   "date": "2017-01-17T15:25:43Z",
   "subject": "Factorial Nested ANOVA?",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>Dear all,</div><div><br></div><div>Is it possible to nest factor Tree inside factors Population and Sex when performing factorial MANOVA with procD.lm function? </div><div><br></div><div>I would like to test for population-specific differences between sexes, but taking in account that leaves from the same Tree are more likely to be similar. </div><div><br></div><div>Best regards,</div><div>Milena</div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "Lbu3UJcbFwAJ",
   "from": "Adams, Dean [EEOBS]",
   "author": "4d71c6e24fb21497",
   "date": "2017-01-17T15:46:31Z",
   "subject": "RE: [geomorph-r-package] Factorial Nested ANOVA?",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<div lang=\"EN-US\" link=\"blue\" vlink=\"purple\">\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><a name=\"m_-5732042911955682372__MailEndCompose\" rel=\"nofollow\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\">Milena,<u></u><u></u></span></a></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\">If by tree you mean those that grow in the forest (as opposed to phylogenetic trees), then yes you can.  For a nested model where B is nested within A:<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\">procD.lm(Y~A/B)<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\">See the help page for advanced.procD.lm for an example in geomorph.<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\"><br>\r\nDean<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\">Dr. Dean C. Adams</span><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\"><u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\">Professor</span><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\"><u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\">Department of Ecology, Evolution, and Organismal Biology</span><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\"><u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\">       Department of Statistics</span><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\"><u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\">Iowa State University</span><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\"><u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><a href=\"http://www.public.iastate.edu/~dcadams/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.public.iastate.edu/~dcadams/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792486186071000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2TggWxuW1Pg3QCUzM7eITD\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:purple\">www.public.iastate.edu/~dcadams/</span></a><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\"><u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\">phone: <a href=\"tel:(515)%20294-3834\" value=\"+15152943834\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\">515-294-3834</a></span><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\"><u></u><u></u></span></p></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div lang=\"EN-US\" link=\"blue\" vlink=\"purple\"><div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><b><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif\">From:</span></b><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif\"> <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">geomorph-...@googlegroups.com</a> [mailto:<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">geomorph-...@googlegroups.com</a>]\r\n<b>On Behalf Of </b>Milena Stefanovic<br>\r\n<b>Sent:</b> Tuesday, January 17, 2017 9:26 AM<br>\r\n<b>To:</b> geomorph R package &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">geomorph-...@googlegroups.com</a>&gt;<br>\r\n<b>Subject:</b> [geomorph-r-package] Factorial Nested ANOVA?<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Dear all,<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Is it possible to nest factor Tree inside factors Population and Sex when performing factorial MANOVA with procD.lm function? <u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">I would like to test for population-specific differences between sexes, but taking in account that leaves from the same Tree are more likely to be similar. <u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Best regards,<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Milena<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div></div>"
