   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Yes, &quot;trees in the forest&quot;.<div><br></div><div>But, is it possible to run procD.lm with 2 main and 1 random effects:</div><div><br></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(31,73,125);font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;font-size:14.6667px\">procD.lm(Y~A/B * C/B)</span></div><div><font color=\"#1f497d\" face=\"Calibri, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14.6667px\"><br></span></font></div><div><font color=\"#1f497d\" face=\"Calibri, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14.6667px\">Thank you,</span></font></div><div><font color=\"#1f497d\" face=\"Calibri, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14.6667px\"><br></span></font>Milena<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div lang=\"EN-US\" link=\"blue\" vlink=\"purple\"><div>\n</div>\n</div>\n\n</blockquote></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "m0KkAOYwFwAJ",
   "from": "Adams, Dean [EEOBS]",
   "author": "4d71c6e24fb21497",
   "date": "2017-01-17T22:16:59Z",
   "subject": "RE: [geomorph-r-package] Factorial Nested ANOVA?",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<div lang=\"EN-US\" link=\"blue\" vlink=\"purple\">\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><a name=\"m_-3907124040522767411__MailEndCompose\" rel=\"nofollow\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\">One cannot have a factor ‘B’ nested in BOTH A and C.  That is simply not possible.  One could have B nested in A, and C nested in B.<u></u><u></u></span></a></p></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
