    [
     1,
     "<div style=\"word-wrap:break-word\">Hi Milena,<div><br></div><div>It is possible to run this something similar to this model, and then use nested.update twice, in succession, to update the F values for the A and C effects.  For example,</div><div><br></div><div>fit &lt;- <span style=\"color:rgb(31,73,125);font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;font-size:14.6667px\">procD.lm(Y~A/B + C/B)</span></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(31,73,125);font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;font-size:14.6667px\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(31,73,125);font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;font-size:14.6667px\">fit &lt;- nested.update(fit, ~A/B)</span></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(31,73,125);font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;font-size:14.6667px\">fit &lt;- nested(update(fit, ~C/B)</span></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(31,73,125);font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;font-size:14.6667px\"><br></span></div><div><font color=\"#1f497d\" face=\"Calibri, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14.66670036315918px\">You can also try </span></font></div><div><font color=\"#1f497d\" face=\"Calibri, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14.66670036315918px\"><br></span></font></div><div><blockquote type=\"cite\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><span style=\"color:rgb(31,73,125);font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;font-size:14.6667px\">procD.lm(Y~ (A*C)/B)</span></div></div></blockquote></div><div><br></div><div>But I do not believe the nested.update function would be useful - it is not capable of handling such complex designs.</div><div><br></div><div>Mike</div><div><br><div><blockquote type=\"cite\"></blockquote></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div style=\"word-wrap:break-word\"><div><div><blockquote type=\"cite\"><div>On Jan 17, 2017, at 4:35 PM, Milena Stefanovic &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">milen...@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:</div><br></blockquote></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div style=\"word-wrap:break-word\"><div><div><blockquote type=\"cite\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\">Yes, &quot;trees in the forest&quot;.<div><br></div><div>But, is it possible to run procD.lm with 2 main and 1 random effects:</div><div><br></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(31,73,125);font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;font-size:14.6667px\">procD.lm(Y~A/B * C/B)</span></div><div><font color=\"#1f497d\" face=\"Calibri, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14.6667px\"><br></span></font></div><div><font color=\"#1f497d\" face=\"Calibri, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14.6667px\">Thank you,</span></font></div><div><font color=\"#1f497d\" face=\"Calibri, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14.6667px\"><br></span></font>Milena<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div lang=\"EN-US\" link=\"blue\" vlink=\"purple\"><div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n</blockquote></div></div><div><br></div></div></blockquote></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<div style=\"word-wrap:break-word\"><div><div><blockquote type=\"cite\"><div>\r\n\r\n-- <br>\r\nYou received this message because you are subscribed to the Google Groups &quot;geomorph R package&quot; group.<br>\r\nTo unsubscribe from this group and stop receiving emails from it, send an email to <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">geomorph-r-pack...@googlegroups.com</a>.<br>\r\nTo post to this group, send email to <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">geomorph-...@googlegroups.com</a>.<br>\r\nVisit this group at <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/group/geomorph-r-package\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/group/geomorph-r-package&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792486186076000&amp;usg=AOvVaw25pjTH8X4m3wpKKOdlPRiU\">https://groups.google.com/group/geomorph-r-package</a>.<br></div></blockquote></div></div></div>"
    ],
