  {
   "id": "oilMQNAyFwAJ",
   "from": "Mike Collyer",
   "author": "aab55242ff4da6c6",
   "date": "2017-01-17T22:52:05Z",
   "subject": "Re: [geomorph-r-package] Factorial Nested ANOVA?",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div style=\"word-wrap:break-word\">Yes, this is a good point that I overlooked when focusing on recursive updates.<div><br></div><div>Maybe what you wish to do, Milena, is make a new factor from your factors A and C?  For example,</div><div><br></div><div>D &lt;- interaction(A, C)</div><div><br></div><div>then</div><div><br></div><div>fit &lt;- procD.lm(Y ~ D/B)</div><div><br></div><div>if B is nested within e.g., experimental treatments defined by combinations of the levels of A and C.</div><div><br></div><div>Mike<br><div><br></div><div><br><div><blockquote type=\"cite\"></blockquote></div></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div style=\"word-wrap:break-word\"><div><div><div><blockquote type=\"cite\"><div>On Jan 17, 2017, at 5:16 PM, Adams, Dean [EEOBS] &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">dca...@iastate.edu</a>&gt; wrote:</div><br></blockquote></div></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div style=\"word-wrap:break-word\"><div><div><div><blockquote type=\"cite\"><div><div style=\"font-family:Helvetica;font-size:12px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px\"><div style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;font-size:12pt;font-family:&#39;Times New Roman&#39;,serif\"><a name=\"m_9010128209339389903__MailEndCompose\" rel=\"nofollow\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(31,73,125)\">One cannot have a factor ‘B’ nested in BOTH A and C.  That is simply not possible.  One could have B nested in A, and C nested in B.<u></u><u></u></span></a></div><div style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;font-size:12pt;font-family:&#39;Times New Roman&#39;,serif\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(31,73,125)\"><br>Dean<span> </span><u></u><u></u></span></div><div style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;font-size:12pt;font-family:&#39;Times New Roman&#39;,serif\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(31,73,125)\"><u></u> <u></u></span></div><div style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;font-size:12pt;font-family:&#39;Times New Roman&#39;,serif\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(31,73,125)\">Dr. Dean C. Adams</span><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(31,73,125)\"><u></u><u></u></span></div><div style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;font-size:12pt;font-family:&#39;Times New Roman&#39;,serif\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(31,73,125)\">Professor</span><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(31,73,125)\"><u></u><u></u></span></div><div style=\"margin:0in 0in 0.0001pt;font-size:12pt;font-family:&#39;Times New Roman&#39;,serif\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(31,73,125)\">Department of Ecology, Evolution, 